      "claim_text": "The pilot coder and the LLM agree on relevance for 97 percent of articles (Table 4), with three relevant articles in the pilot.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Section 3.1.4 states manual coding yielded five relevant articles, of which two were reclassified for the validation. Footnote 2 on page 7 says the same. The paper does not show agreement under the original definition or whether the LLM was independently instructed to exclude pre-opening articles. Table 4 implies the LLM flagged 4 relevant, consistent with the recoded set plus the Stord article, but this does not show agreement was insensitive to the recoding. With so few positives, treating two articles differently changes the positive class by 40%.",
