        "page": 7,
        "page_label": "7",
        "section": "4 Validation",
        "text_quote": "The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "None of the human coding was included in the LLM prompt. The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Section 3.2 says the output quality was reviewed after the first run and the prompt altered, including a broadening of relevant infrastructure. It then says 'After updating the prompt, the analysis of the validation set of articles was repeated.' The prompt-development loop therefore used the same 34 articles later used for the headline agreement. The paper does not say whether the validation set also informed prompt changes beyond geography, or give the agreement before the revision. The claim that the prompt change 'did not make a difference' is asserted without reported results. Hence the 97% is not clean out-of-sample evidence.",
