        "text_quote": "internal consistency of the first-stage coding (relevant vs. not relevant).",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "Out of 34 articles, only one (3%) showed disagreement between coding runs. This was deemed a sufficiently high level of internal consistency.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "The check is stated for first-stage relevance only. The 3% disagreement is the single borderline Stord article, and the 97% in Table 4 uses the majority of three runs, so single-run agreement is not reported. The abstract's 29 projects dated to the day or month and the 'same opening date' claim depend on date extraction, whose stability across runs is not shown. The paper does not state whether the 3,187-article run used one pass or repeated passes with the default temperature.",
