      "claim_text": "The share has increased over the period, from about 35 percent in 2020 to about 44 percent at the end of the period, although with some variation between quarters and a dip in the second half of 2023. (Section 6.1: the share mentioning cycling has risen by about 9 percentage points over the period.)",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Reading Figure 3 visually (values approximate), quarterly shares run about 35% to about 38–39% in 2020–2023 and fall to about 33.5% in Q4 2023. After the Jan–Apr 2024 gap they resume at about 39% and rise to about 44%. The upward shift therefore coincides with the missing data, so a composition or data-source break cannot be ruled out. The caption says January to April 2024 is missing, while the text says only the first quarter is missing. The first plotted post-gap point appears to be Q2 2024, which would then rest on a partial quarter. The paper reports no trend estimate, no adjustment for listing composition or text length, and no check on whether the post-gap source is comparable.",
