      "evidence_summary": "In Table 9 (read from page text, not the structured CSV) Parking & storage, which contains “stativ” (rack), is listed before Infrastructure, which contains “bysykkel”. Under the stated first-in-table rule, bysykkelstativ would be Parking & storage, not infrastructure. Likewise “syklende” contains “sykle”, listed under Proximity before Infrastructure, yet Figure 2 colours both bysykkelstativ and syklende as Infrastructure (blue). The statement of the rule and its application therefore disagree. This establishes a documentation inconsistency, not which rule was implemented. The effect on Table 8 type shares is probably small (these words are about 0.5% and 0.3% of listings), but it bears on the infrastructure-versus-parking ordering reported in the text. The authors also say the classification 'is thus coarse', and no validation of it is given.",
